A: Table 15: Descriptive fake-data numbers, none of them a test result. In-sample: against Ctotal + Cresp including the truth’s own generator shift, which is not evidence (— where the test already uses the full matrix). Model-only: against the statistical block and Cmodel without the truth’s own generator shift, omitting the interaction, flux, detector, lateral and normalization blocks, so a lower bound on Cmodel ’s reach. Power alternatives: the NuWro (pT , p∥ , Eavail ) shape (P1), a NuWro q3 shape at fixed (Eavail , W ) (P2) and the GENIE + MEC (Eavail , W ) shape (P3), each on the Tune v1 truth (r) and on the GENIE CV truth (g).
B: TABLE IV: Triangular discriminator values from comparing unfolded differential cross sections using each method to the truth-level cross sections underlying the data. Results are divided by observable of interest.
